<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint-Cloud</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint-Cloud is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a> west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, named after the Merovingian prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clodoald">Clodoald</a>, Saint Cloud, who founded a monastery there in the 6th century. Its château, built by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a> branch of the French royal family, was a residence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>, who seized power at Saint-Cloud in the coup of 18 Brumaire in 1799. The château was burnt in 1870, but its park remains.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saint-cloud.jpg" alt="Saint-Cloud" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Moonik · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint-Cloud_Town_Hall_002.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
